    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0523" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.00 Revolutions/389: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at São
                        Paulo</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cameron</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-27T18:00:00-05:00">September 27,
                            1932—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your September 24, 2 p.m. If, as the Department understands, the Brazilian
                    Government is maintaining an actual, effective blockade of the port of Santos,
                    this Government cannot protest as requested by the American Chamber of
                    Commerce.</p>
                <p>Inform Embassy.</p>
                <p>The Department feels that it cannot properly forward the resolution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
